  "term": "alpha rhythm",
  "definition": "Alpha rhythm is a pattern of brain-wave activity with relatively high amplitude and a frequency of 8 to 13 hertz. It is commonly seen on an EEG over the parietal and occipital areas when a person is awake, relaxed, and has their eyes closed.",
